### AB small (3k rows/fetch): worker_cpu 97.92 -> 87.62 ns/row (-10.30, -10.5%; -30.9 us per 3000-row fetch), worker 106.61 -> 97.97 (-8.64, -8.1%; -25.9 us/fetch), total 194.33 -> 184.53 (-9.80, -5.0%; 5.15M -> 5.42M rows/s, +5.3%)
### AB control (100k rows/fetch): worker_cpu 44.60 -> 43.01 (-1.59, -3.6%; run ranges 44.15-44.71 vs 42.16-45.29: flat), worker 37.87 -> 37.86 (-0.0%), total 325.26 -> 317.05 (client-side noise, -2.5%)

## control: the official 100k benchmark, three runs per side
#
# `docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=<side> fpq-<side>
#  benchmarks.sh 100000`, medians of three. Its spread is ±10% run to run, so
# both path numbers moving in opposite directions is noise, not the change:
#   stream()   8.74M -> 8.92M rows/s (+2.1%)
#   DBAPI      3.76M -> 3.72M rows/s (-1.1%)
